[0;36m[2026-08-25 17:47:16][0m Committing: "fix(auth): remove school selector from login — it locked every parent out

With more than one active school the login page required a school. Parents have
school_id = NULL and no user_school_access rows, so canAccessSchool() returned
false for every option and AuthController logged them straight back out with
'You do not have access to that school'. 23 of 24 production parents were
affected and could not reach the portal at all.

The field was redundant: the backend already returns school_id and
accessible_school_ids on login, and multi-school users pick their school from the
existing header switcher. Login is now email + password only.

Deliberately NOT implemented: looking the email up as it is typed to decide
whether to show the field. An unauthenticated endpoint answering 'does this email
exist and is it multi-school' is a user-enumeration oracle that also reveals which
accounts are admins.

The backend school gate is unchanged and still rejects a school the user cannot
access, for any client that still sends school_id.

Also hides the header school switcher from parents — /api/schools returns all
active schools to any authenticated user, so they were being offered a switcher
that does nothing for them."
