[0;36m[2026-08-27 09:47:32][0m Committing: "fix(ui): clean up CoreUI modal artefacts that froze the interface

Two defects in @coreui/vue v5 CModal made the UI appear stuck until reload.

1. Orphaned backdrops. CBackdrop renders inside a CSS-class <Transition>. When
   the leave transition is interrupted — trivial on pages that mount several
   modals — it never completes and the node survives as
   position:fixed inset:0 z-index:1050 opacity:0 pointer-events:auto:
   an invisible sheet over the viewport that swallows every click while the page
   looks entirely normal. Reproduced: two modals open, dismiss one, and
   elementFromPoint at the centre returns the backdrop with the toolbar button
   unreachable.

2. Stale scroll lock. CModal writes modal-open and overflow:hidden onto <body>
   in its Transition enter hook and only reverses that in the leave hook. It has
   no onUnmounted, so navigating away with a modal open leaves the page unable to
   scroll permanently, and leaks a window mousedown + keydown listener per
   occurrence (measured: 1, 2, 3 across three cycles).

Adds utils/modalGuard.js, which reconciles the DOM instead of forking the
dependency: backdrops may never outnumber visible modals, and with nothing open
there is no backdrop and no scroll lock. Triggered by a MutationObserver
(class/style included, since closing a modal only toggles v-show), the router
afterEach, and a capture-phase click on any backdrop as a self-heal.

Verified an open modal keeps its backdrop, so dimming still works."
