[0;36m[2026-08-27 19:37:01][0m Committing: "fix(pdf): logo never rendered; portrait viewer; statement fits any invoice count

Logo: BrandingController uploads with ->store(..., 'public') but the letterhead
read it with a bare Storage::exists(), which uses the default disk
(FILESYSTEM_DISK, unset here so 'local'). That checked storage/app/ while the
file sits in storage/app/public/, so exists() was always false and the logo was
silently dropped from every PDF. Confirmed on production: default disk false,
public disk true. Now reads the public disk explicitly and tolerates the legacy
'public/' prefix.

Motto now prints in italic capitals, the convention on school letterhead.

Viewer: the frame stretched to the full modal width, leaving a portrait page as a
small block in a wide grey field. It is now an A-series portrait box (measured
0.707) with view=Fit so the page fills it, falling back to full width on phones.

Consolidated statement: overflowed to a second page from 12 invoices — four per
year means a pupil of six years reaches 24. Density now steps up before anything
is hidden (payments summarised past 6, condensed rows past 6) and only the oldest
collapse into one carried-forward row past 14. Verified single page from 4 to 40."
