[0;36m[2026-08-28 16:43:09][0m Committing: "feat(dashboard): per-user privacy lock for money figures

The three money cards (Outstanding Debt, Paid Invoices, Today's Collections)
and the Fee Collection Summary by Class can be hidden behind a code each user
sets for themselves.

Redaction happens server-side, not in the browser: while locked the API omits
those values entirely and marks the payload locked:true, so there is nothing to
recover from the network response. The frontend only decides how to draw the
absence, showing dots instead of the 0 it would otherwise compute.

Keys are redacted by VALUE rather than by which card shows them --
/dashibodi renders the same collections and debt from total_collected_cents /
total_outstanding_cents, so redacting only the /dashboard keys would leave the
lock bypassable by opening the other page. The outstanding-debts spreadsheet
export is gated by the same rule for the same reason.

Per user: each superadmin, owner and accountant sets an independent code, and
one user locking never affects a colleague. Only a bcrypt hash is stored.
Unlocking grants a 5-minute server-side pass that expires on its own. Unlock
attempts are rate-limited (a 4-digit code falls in seconds otherwise), and a
forgotten code is cleared with the account password.

Existing logic untouched: DashboardService is not modified, and student
registration and every other write path are unaffected -- covered by test.

13 new tests, full suite 28 passed."
