[0;36m[2026-08-28 18:19:09][0m Committing: "fix(dashboard): withhold trend and breakdown amounts under the privacy lock

The Collection Trend Analysis chart kept plotting the very figures the cards
above it were hiding — the final bar of weekly_trend IS today's collections, so
a locked dashboard showed 66.8M in a graph while the card read dots.

Extends the redaction set to every remaining money-bearing key: weekly_trend,
payment_trend, method_breakdown, recent_payments and top_debtors (the last two
also pair a student name with an amount), plus paid_amount_cents,
total_expenses_cents and collection_rate. class_breakdown and school_breakdown
stay — they are enrollment counts, and the lock hides money, not the school.

Dashibodi's monthly-expenses card and collection-rate gauge mask too, and the
trend chart shows a lock chip so an empty chart does not read as a load failure.

New test asserts none of the stubbed amounts appear anywhere in the serialised
payload while locked. Full suite 29 passed."
